11
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Colonel Mustard, played by Martin Mull.

12
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Clue is a 1985 American black comedy mystery film based on the
board game Clue (Cluedo outside North America).

13
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:12,000
It was written and directed by Jonathan Lynn, who
co-wrote the story with John Landis.

14
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
It features an ensemble cast, including Eileen Brennan, Tim Curry, Madeline Kahn,
Christopher Lloyd, Michael McKean, Martin Mull, and Lesley Ann Warren.

15
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
The film has multiple different endings.

16
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
Each of three possibilities were screened at different
theaters, and home media releases include all of them.

17
01:19:54,000 --> 01:20:00,000
The film initially received mixed reviews and performed poorly at the box office, grossing $15 million in
the United States against a budget of $15 million, but later developed a cult following.

18
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
The film explores themes of blackmail, butler, board game, mansion, whodunit.

19
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:24,000
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending and intense.
